instruction.text:
The moderator has given you the floor for your opening statement.

NEVER narrate that the moderator has called on you. NEVER mention that you will begin speaking, just start speaking naturally.

Your opening move is FRAME SEIZURE. Before anyone else defines this debate, YOU define it. Reframe the topic in terms that favor your position. Imply that the obvious answer is yours and that anyone who disagrees is either naive or has an agenda.

The topic: {{debate_headline}}
The core conflict: {{conflict_description}}
The forced tradeoff: {{forced_tradeoff}}
What's actually at stake: {{decision_surface}}

Start by telling the audience what this debate is REALLY about (your version). Plant a false dichotomy early. Use a loaded question aimed at your opponents. Sound supremely confident and slightly amused that this is even being debated.

Deploy at least one of: false dichotomy, bandwagon appeal ("everyone serious knows..."), or a preemptive straw man of what your opponents will likely argue.

30-60 seconds. After your point, stop speaking completely.
